+# Art direction — illustrated 2.5D shop overview selected
 
-## Art Target
+The [V1a reference board](../05-reference/presentation-choice-2026-09-07.md) records the owner’s exact selection “B”: Kardboard Kings illustrated 2.5D overview, using editable Krita masters/cleanup and Godot animation. Official motion examples are linked; their playback/timecodes are not verified.
 
-Hybrid stylized realism.
+Only the retail loop is retained. The selected presentation is an illustrated 2.5D shop overview. Palette, era, original assets, environment, interface and exact camera treatment remain to be developed; the reference does not lock these details.
 
-The game should feel grounded in early-2000s retail while staying readable, performant, and slightly stylized like a modern simulator.
+| Approach | Retail opportunity | Cost/risk to prove first |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Illustrated 2D | Clear customer silhouettes and composed shelf/counter views; stock and sales can use direct selection | Motion and directional identity at small scale; readable handling without relying on close-ups; layered cutout gaps or authored-frame workload |
+| Angled / 2.5D | Store overview makes shelf gaps and customer routes visible together | Feet staying planted, facing changes, sorting behind/in front of fixtures, depth consistency and product selection under overlap |
+| 3D | Spatial browsing, flexible viewpoints and close inspection can make stock handling tactile | Character rig/turn quality, consistent stylization and lighting at chosen distance, occlusion and camera usability; extra asset work must earn a gameplay advantage |
 
-The next production phase is visual-first. The first 0.3% of the game must look right before additional gameplay breadth is added.
+These are alternatives; the board now recommends B without committing the owner. Camera choice remains independent: 3D does not imply first-person, and 2.5D must be specified precisely (for example, sprites in a 3D scene versus layered 2D).
 
-## Mood
+Reference boards must use actual attributable images and motion clips, not style adjectives or generated aspirational mockups. For each candidate record source URL/file, creator/title, capture/timecode, what we would borrow as a principle, intended camera and character screen size, and how stocking, customers, and sales read. References are not permission to copy assets. Select one primary target with owner input before production.
 
-Warm nostalgia:
+Record palette, linework, proportions, shading, texture, motion and camera rules from that reference. Existing Blender assets and inspiration folders are optional. The space-opera RPG experience informs test discipline only.
 
-- bright mall lighting
-- familiar retail materials
-- clean but slightly busy surfaces
-- colorful product faces
-- visible shelf gaps early
-- cardboard and plastic tactility
-- inviting small-shop atmosphere
-
-## Real Reference Extraction
-
-Use `real_inspiration/` for:
-
-- wire-grid shelving
-- acrylic case rows
-- platform/category strips
