+- Keep editable sources: layered `.kra` for illustrated masters, `.blend` or equivalent for a 3D source, plus rig/animation sources. Keep one character identity master, revision identities, exports and provenance/usage rights.
+- Inspect actual alpha-channel values and composite exports over contrasting backgrounds. A painted checkerboard is not transparency. Record alpha as not applicable for opaque assets rather than silently skipping the check.
+- Record dimensions, pivots, layer order, reconstructed hidden surfaces, world/display scale, export/import settings, engine version, and exact code/asset revisions.
+- Retain real engine captures and a short motion recording. Synthetic pixel-painted images and successful imports are technical artifacts only.
+- Re-export from the editable master, reimport, and relaunch the same scene once to demonstrate repeatability.
+- Let the owner operate the moving sample. Preserve exact feedback separately from defect results.
 
