+# Game Store Sim — current master plan
 
-This is the primary production reference for Game Store Sim. When implementation starts, this document should remain the first file engineers, designers, artists, and testers read.
+Updated: 2026-09-07. Restart preparation complete; visual direction B selected by owner.
 
-The purpose of this plan is to turn the current game-guide canon and inspiration folders into an implementation-ready first playable without losing the larger game fantasy.
+## Intent
 
-## 1. Product Thesis
+Recover the player loop: prepare the store, receive and price stock, stock shelves, open, serve customers, make sales, close, review results, and decide what to do next. Preserve meaningful choices and coherent inventory, money, and results. No existing implementation is mandatory.
 
-Game Store Sim is a first-person retail life sim about operating one believable independent game store in an early-2000s mall.
+Art, assets, camera, interface, presentation, and dimensional approach can restart. First-person, 3D, mall setting, era, palette, one rendered object per stock item, and historical progression rules are not locked requirements. Illustrated 2D, 2.5D, and 3D must be evaluated on their merits. Logical stock identity can survive any rendering approach.
 
-The game is not about becoming a giant chain, collecting real-world brands, or solving a separate mystery campaign. It is about touching the daily work of a small game shop:
+Godot 4.6.2 Standard with GDScript and Compatibility is the available starting tool, not a visual constraint. Choose tools according to the small proof's demonstrated needs.
 
-- receiving stock
-- checking invoices
-- pricing used goods
-- stocking visible shelves
-- helping customers
-- keeping launch promises
-- handling returns and services
-- ordering from suppliers
-- reading daily reports
-- deciding what kind of store this is becoming
+## Current facts
 
-The long-term fantasy is:
+The recovered source has a one-day technical prototype and separate static visual benchmark assets. It does not implement a repeatable retail business. Read the [recovery review](03-production/recovery-review-2026-09-07.md) for exact scope and failures. Historical successful exports, screenshots, and completion claims are not current verification or acceptance.
 
-> I opened this place myself. Every shelf tells me what I chose, what I missed, and what I am trying to become.
